WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.702
There are twelve of them.

00:00:05.424 --> 00:00:08.246
twelve stadiums built in the four corners of Europe,

00:00:11.009 --> 00:00:16.635
imagined by the most daring architects and built by thousands of workers and engineers.

00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:21.939
Twelve gigantic arenas,

00:00:22.719 --> 00:00:26.041
Selected to host matches for a global event,

00:00:26.981 --> 00:00:29.062
the 2020 European Football Championship.

00:00:31.984 --> 00:00:33.945
Embarking on a unique tour of Europe,

00:00:34.905 --> 00:00:37.307
Discovering the most beautiful stadiums on the continent.

00:01:01.856 --> 00:01:02.657
In this episode,

00:01:03.036 --> 00:01:04.317
the match will pit.

00:01:05.739 --> 00:01:10.722
The Gazprom Arena in Saint Petersburg, Russia, to the Olympic Stadium in Baku, Azerbaijan.

00:01:28.843 --> 00:01:29.263
On one hand,

00:01:29.824 --> 00:01:31.585
an arena resembling a flying saucer,

00:01:31.945 --> 00:01:34.406
whose construction required more than 10 years of work,

00:01:34.947 --> 00:01:37.588
equipped with a retractable roof and a removable lawn,

00:01:38.068 --> 00:01:39.949
and which is home to one of the biggest clubs in Europe,

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:41.610
Zenit Saint Petersburg.

00:01:45.673 --> 00:01:47.033
This stadium is truly fantastic.

00:01:47.914 --> 00:01:49.735
And the acoustics are so impressive.

00:01:51.576 --> 00:01:51.697
Me,

00:01:51.777 --> 00:01:52.936
when I step onto the lawn,

00:01:53.358 --> 00:01:55.838
I feel a bit like I'm in a huge theatre.

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:02.040
On the other hand,

00:02:02.579 --> 00:02:05.641
a venue that has already hosted the biggest European finals.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:08.722
With architecture inspired by a 12th-century tower,

00:02:09.461 --> 00:02:13.182
capable of withstanding the strongest winds and earthquakes,

00:02:13.823 --> 00:02:16.264
and which was built in barely two years.

00:02:18.084 --> 00:02:21.485
The Baku Olympic Stadium is the largest stadium in the Caucasus region.

00:02:21.925 --> 00:02:23.846
A venue with a capacity of 68,000 people.

00:02:24.186 --> 00:02:25.826
Given the number of components to be manufactured,

00:02:26.206 --> 00:02:28.706
Meeting construction deadlines was our biggest challenge.

00:02:31.168 --> 00:02:32.969
A head-to-head between two stadiums,

00:02:33.350 --> 00:02:35.793
located at the crossroads between Europe and Asia,

00:02:36.254 --> 00:02:38.657
and which are among the most modern speakers in the world.

00:03:00.247 --> 00:03:05.792
Let us begin our journey on the shores of the Gulf of the Baltic Sea, where the city of Saint Petersburg stands.

00:03:07.332 --> 00:03:08.633
Nicknamed the Venice of the North,

00:03:09.214 --> 00:03:13.018
The city was founded in 1703 on the marshy mouth of the Neva River.

00:03:15.819 --> 00:03:16.199
Today,

00:03:16.881 --> 00:03:18.281
with its 5 million inhabitants,

00:03:18.721 --> 00:03:20.923
It has become the second largest city in Russia after Moscow.

00:03:23.856 --> 00:03:25.877
The city previously had two stadiums.

00:03:26.578 --> 00:03:27.038
The first,

00:03:27.479 --> 00:03:28.439
Petrovsky Stadium,

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:30.301
located on the island of the same name.

00:03:31.762 --> 00:03:33.423
An old stadium with a capacity of 22,000,

00:03:33.643 --> 00:03:35.044
built in 1925,

00:03:35.524 --> 00:03:39.367
which hosted FC Zenit Saint Petersburg matches for several decades.

00:03:40.848 --> 00:03:41.228
The other one,

00:03:41.729 --> 00:03:42.549
Kirov Stadium,

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.471
located less than 4 km away,

00:03:45.871 --> 00:03:47.753
on another island of barely more than 3 km²,

00:03:48.834 --> 00:03:50.134
surrounded by the arms of the Neva.

00:03:50.835 --> 00:03:51.656
Krestovski Island.

00:03:53.204 --> 00:03:54.665
Inaugurated in 1950,

00:03:55.186 --> 00:03:57.588
The stadium could accommodate up to 110,000 people.

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:05.418
It is on the site of the old Kirov stadium that the authorities have decided to build an ultra-modern stadium for the city's club to play in.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.941
It was named the Gazprom Arena.

00:04:20.843 --> 00:04:23.906
The enclosure came straight from the imagination of the Japanese architect.

00:04:24.307 --> 00:04:25.107
Kisho Kurokawa,

00:04:25.608 --> 00:04:26.328
now deceased,

00:04:26.809 --> 00:04:29.311
but considered one of the greatest architects in the world.

00:04:30.951 --> 00:04:31.632
Among his achievements,

00:04:31.872 --> 00:04:33.734
among his most notable achievements,

00:04:34.274 --> 00:04:35.574
the Nakagin capsule tower,

00:04:36.536 --> 00:04:38.297
the Tokyo National Arts Center,

00:04:39.899 --> 00:04:40.459
but above all,

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:42.199
Oita Stadium,

00:04:42.860 --> 00:04:45.083
built for the 2002 FIFA World Cup.

00:04:47.103 --> 00:04:49.127
Featuring the largest retractable roof in the country,

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:53.612
This arena with its exceptional design has been nicknamed the Big Eye.

00:04:55.173 --> 00:04:56.035
Even back then,

00:04:56.456 --> 00:05:00.000
Kisho Kurokawa had proven to the world his originality and his ability to do things.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.221
It drew inspiration from the most unexpected models.

00:05:03.543 --> 00:05:08.946
And the shape of the Gazprom Arena in Saint Petersburg is further proof of the architect's inventiveness.

00:05:25.351 --> 00:05:28.473
His vision was to give the stadium the appearance of a flying saucer.

00:05:29.433 --> 00:05:30.493
The shape of the stadium,

00:05:31.594 --> 00:05:32.014
the roof,

00:05:32.495 --> 00:05:33.194
the windows,

00:05:33.754 --> 00:05:34.495
the stairs,

00:05:35.216 --> 00:05:40.137
Everything has been designed so that the enclosure resembles an extraterrestrial UFO point by point.

00:05:46.640 --> 00:05:51.842
Yuji Imayo was part of the team that designed this stadium under the direction of Kisho Kurokawa.

00:05:58.825 --> 00:05:59.225
First of all,

00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:01.206
This stadium has a circular shape.

00:06:01.848 --> 00:06:02.687
whereas usually,

00:06:02.728 --> 00:06:06.010
Football stadiums are usually elliptical or rectangular in shape.

00:06:07.651 --> 00:06:08.072
This time,

00:06:08.872 --> 00:06:11.233
Kurokawa gave the enclosure the shape of a stadium.

00:06:12.716 --> 00:06:15.478
This is the main reason that gives it this spaceship-like appearance.

00:06:17.721 --> 00:06:18.041
And then,

00:06:18.181 --> 00:06:20.144
There are also these very special windows.

00:06:20.825 --> 00:06:26.192
I remember Kurokawa repeatedly making me correct my plans, pointing out that I probably hadn't done that.

00:06:26.192 --> 00:06:27.973
Probably never seen a UFO window.

00:06:32.615 --> 00:06:33.055
And finally,

00:06:33.074 --> 00:06:33.935
There are stairs.

00:06:34.435 --> 00:06:34.775
Today,

00:06:34.795 --> 00:06:35.475
They are fixed.

00:06:35.656 --> 00:06:36.256
but initially,

00:06:36.316 --> 00:06:37.997
We wanted them to be retractable.

00:06:38.896 --> 00:06:42.679
A bit like when a UFO hatch opens to let the crew out.

00:06:48.413 --> 00:06:50.494
The day after the presentation of our project,

00:06:51.295 --> 00:06:55.978
We could read on the front page of the city's newspapers that a UFO was going to land in Saint Petersburg.

00:07:02.661 --> 00:07:06.524
We hadn't yet told anyone that we had used a spaceship as our model.

00:07:07.365 --> 00:07:09.646
It was hoped that people would discover it for themselves.

00:07:10.747 --> 00:07:11.608
And that was the case.

00:07:11.668 --> 00:07:14.411
So it was a great victory for us.

00:07:25.351 --> 00:07:26.612
I think that where he is,

00:07:27.173 --> 00:07:32.197
Kurokawa is watching us from his spaceship and he is really very happy.

00:07:33.259 --> 00:07:35.219
And I think he thanks everyone from the bottom of his heart.

00:07:55.968 --> 00:07:58.788
While a perfectly circular stadium was extremely rare at the time,

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:01.350
There's another one that's recently appeared.

00:08:06.471 --> 00:08:09.213
Located 3000 km southeast of Saint Petersburg,

00:08:09.713 --> 00:08:11.555
in a country located between Europe and Asia,

00:08:13.094 --> 00:08:13.814
Azerbaijan.

00:08:15.911 --> 00:08:16.432
It's in Baku,

00:08:16.872 --> 00:08:18.394
capital city of 2 million inhabitants,

00:08:18.933 --> 00:08:20.915
which was inaugurated in 2015,

00:08:20.916 --> 00:08:22.557
in the heart of the city's new districts,

00:08:23.036 --> 00:08:24.017
the Olympic stadium.

00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:30.822
This uniquely designed venue has become one of the country's new architectural prides.

00:08:33.624 --> 00:08:36.145
The stadium was designed by the architects at ERIM.

00:08:36.525 --> 00:08:38.206
a prestigious South Korean firm.

00:08:39.207 --> 00:08:39.808
Their objective?

00:08:40.668 --> 00:08:45.533
To rediscover in this new building the traces of the country's glorious past and the symbols of the city.

00:08:47.195 --> 00:08:47.695
Because Baku,

00:08:48.335 --> 00:08:50.096
located on the shores of the Caspian Sea,

00:08:50.537 --> 00:08:53.139
was previously known primarily for its medieval city,

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:54.120
its ramparts,

00:08:54.340 --> 00:08:56.422
its minarets and its magnificent palaces.

00:09:01.409 --> 00:09:02.731
When this stadium was designed,

00:09:03.012 --> 00:09:04.594
which is the largest stadium in Azerbaijan,

00:09:05.476 --> 00:09:08.200
We first had to decide what it could look like.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.882
He was supposed to represent the country,

00:09:10.103 --> 00:09:13.488
So we asked ourselves what element should serve as our inspiration.

00:09:15.575 --> 00:09:17.937
The main source of inspiration for architects,

00:09:18.476 --> 00:09:18.896
It's her.

00:09:19.716 --> 00:09:20.538
Maiden Tower,

00:09:21.197 --> 00:09:22.477
known as the Virgin's Tower.

00:09:23.557 --> 00:09:26.418
Built in the 12th century and standing about thirty meters tall,

00:09:27.019 --> 00:09:32.780
The building, a UNESCO World Heritage Site, has now become one of the city's emblems, known throughout the world.

00:09:42.115 --> 00:09:44.439
The stadium was therefore designed to resemble the Maiden Tower.

00:09:44.879 --> 00:09:46.861
in a perfectly cylindrical shape.

00:09:48.403 --> 00:09:52.149
The facade was then designed in the same spirit as that of the 12th-century tower.

00:09:52.769 --> 00:09:56.295
whose walls are composed of a succession of projecting grey limestone stones,

00:09:57.135 --> 00:09:59.459
alternating with recessed gypsum plaster.

00:10:00.880 --> 00:10:05.083
A structure that gives the impression that the tower is composed of black and white stripes.

00:10:07.405 --> 00:10:10.268
So it was this same principle that was reproduced on the stadium.

00:10:11.448 --> 00:10:13.711
But instead of preserving the rectangular shape of the bricks,

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:18.293
This time the architects opted for diamond-shaped panels.

00:10:24.712 --> 00:10:27.315
The diamond motif is also a symbol of fire.

00:10:29.696 --> 00:10:32.378
And since Azerbaijan is known as the land of fire,

00:10:33.318 --> 00:10:37.321
We thought we could bring together the two great symbols of the country with the stadium.

00:10:37.322 --> 00:10:37.701
The first,

00:10:37.702 --> 00:10:38.402
It is the symbol of fire.

00:10:38.402 --> 00:10:38.581
The first,

00:10:38.583 --> 00:10:42.347
It is the facade that recalls the succession of bricks of the Maiden Tower and the second,

00:10:42.507 --> 00:10:44.250
the symbol of fire which represents the country.

00:10:46.993 --> 00:10:52.019
Public access to the stadium was designed with reference to another emblem of Azerbaijan,

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:53.862
the Cannes palace.

00:10:57.915 --> 00:10:58.896
Located in the north of the country,

00:10:59.136 --> 00:11:00.476
300 km from Baku,

00:11:01.317 --> 00:11:03.639
This palace was the summer residence of the Kans.

00:11:04.078 --> 00:11:07.480
rulers of the former feudal state of the Caucasus in the 18th century.

00:11:08.881 --> 00:11:11.783
Renowned worldwide for the colours of its façades and its stained glass windows,

00:11:12.384 --> 00:11:14.684
It features windows known as shabaka windows.

00:11:15.264 --> 00:11:16.985
made of fragments of glass and wood,

00:11:17.365 --> 00:11:18.726
assembled without glue or nails.

00:11:20.447 --> 00:11:24.272
It was their motif that inspired the architects to design the arrival at the stadium.

00:11:25.373 --> 00:11:33.721
The three access ramps leading to the central enclosure are like three wooden axes that cross the circle of glass in the stained-glass windows of the Palais des Cannes.

00:11:40.023 --> 00:11:49.290
The Baku stadium, like that of Saint Petersburg, is therefore among the rare perfectly circular venues, and their original design makes them unique structures in the world.

00:11:51.391 --> 00:11:54.093
But one of them has something special that the other does not.

00:11:55.034 --> 00:12:00.958
The Gazprom Arena has a retractable roof, the design of which required several years of work.

00:12:10.892 --> 00:12:12.451
Because in the heart of the Venice of the North,

00:12:12.812 --> 00:12:13.993
this exceptional city,

00:12:14.853 --> 00:12:18.514
A stadium was needed that could withstand the extreme conditions of the Far North.

00:12:20.735 --> 00:12:20.935
Here,

00:12:20.975 --> 00:12:21.455
in winter,

00:12:22.095 --> 00:12:27.317
Temperatures regularly fall below minus 20 degrees and snow and wind are omnipresent.

00:12:28.856 --> 00:12:30.998
The stadium was therefore equipped with a retractable roof,

00:12:31.798 --> 00:12:38.200
a transparent dome 150 meters in diameter which allows the venue to be used regardless of the weather.

00:12:53.932 --> 00:12:56.836
Nicolas Yegorenko is the stadium's technical director.

00:12:58.038 --> 00:13:00.322
He takes us inside the very structure of the roof,

00:13:00.942 --> 00:13:03.866
where the opening system for this giant dome is located.

00:13:08.629 --> 00:13:08.809
Here,

00:13:08.909 --> 00:13:10.410
we are at the highest point,

00:13:10.530 --> 00:13:13.913
just under the retractable roof which actually consists of two parts.

00:13:14.574 --> 00:13:14.914
Today,

00:13:15.014 --> 00:13:18.717
We opened the roof for the first time since the end of the long winter period.

00:13:19.658 --> 00:13:19.778
There,

00:13:19.838 --> 00:13:23.081
We are in the testing phase to verify that everything works perfectly.

00:13:23.641 --> 00:13:27.625
It takes between 20 and 40 minutes for the roof to open completely.

00:13:31.369 --> 00:13:33.691
The dome is composed of four distinct parts.

00:13:34.848 --> 00:13:40.270
Two that remain fixed and two others that can slide on rails propelled by electric trolleys.

00:13:46.133 --> 00:13:46.613
In total,

00:13:47.313 --> 00:13:51.115
28 trolleys are needed to open and close the two moving parts of the roof.

00:13:58.995 --> 00:14:01.519
An ingenious system that allows you to preserve,

00:14:01.658 --> 00:14:04.120
regardless of the weather conditions outside,

00:14:04.660 --> 00:14:07.264
a temperature of 15 degrees inside the enclosure.

00:14:13.169 --> 00:14:17.533
The temperature in the stadium is maintained using the same principle as that of major airports.

00:14:17.973 --> 00:14:23.198
A ventilation system sends warm air inside and helps to maintain a constant temperature.

00:14:25.091 --> 00:14:31.614
The dome was also specially designed to support the weight of snow in winter and prevent it from accumulating on the roof.

00:14:35.435 --> 00:14:38.615
It is made of a thermoplastic material called ETFE.

00:14:39.536 --> 00:14:41.196
Lighter and much cheaper than glass,

00:14:41.516 --> 00:14:42.777
but extremely durable.

00:14:43.576 --> 00:14:46.498
And very often used in the construction of megastadiums.

00:14:56.514 --> 00:15:00.000
The dome is a

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:01.539
A kind of transparent membrane.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:05.902
The moving part is composed of two separate layers that form a chamber which is pressurized.

00:15:06.562 --> 00:15:11.543
The machines inject compressed air inside and the roof is thus inflated a bit like a balloon.

00:15:17.024 --> 00:15:17.664
In addition to that,

00:15:18.024 --> 00:15:25.246
The spherical shape of the roof makes it even more difficult for snow to accumulate on the dome in winter because the wind makes it slide off the flat surface.

00:15:26.006 --> 00:15:27.687
And if on certain parts of the roof,

00:15:27.988 --> 00:15:29.807
It does accumulate a little in all cases.

00:15:29.807 --> 00:15:30.067
The cases,

00:15:30.168 --> 00:15:31.169
It will eventually melt.

00:15:32.072 --> 00:15:34.895
Because the hot air inside the enclosure tends to rise,

00:15:35.577 --> 00:15:36.840
He will arrive under the dome.

00:15:37.400 --> 00:15:38.663
Since the dome is not insulated,

00:15:39.183 --> 00:15:41.668
The warm air will heat it and melt the snow.

00:15:51.148 --> 00:15:56.111
But this retractable roof system forced architects and engineers to innovate,

00:15:56.511 --> 00:15:59.975
because this area of ​​71,000 m² is a heavy burden.

00:16:00.995 --> 00:16:01.495
Very heavy.

00:16:05.139 --> 00:16:08.321
15,000 tonnes for the circular roof and its transparent dome.

00:16:09.722 --> 00:16:12.884
26,000 for the metal structure on which it rests.

00:16:13.765 --> 00:16:15.667
The equivalent of the weight of 4 Eiffel Towers.

00:16:16.823 --> 00:16:17.924
To support the whole thing,

00:16:18.485 --> 00:16:22.548
It was impossible to use interior pillars that would obstruct the spectators' view.

00:16:23.808 --> 00:16:28.812
The designers therefore used techniques usually employed for the construction of water bridges.

00:16:30.413 --> 00:16:31.693
They installed it on top of the pool,

00:16:31.713 --> 00:16:32.253
At the top of the stadium,

00:16:32.813 --> 00:16:36.134
8 pylons that pass through the roof and are anchored to the ground.

00:16:37.794 --> 00:16:38.535
At their summit,

00:16:39.035 --> 00:16:43.556
Each one of them is equipped with tensioned cables that allow it to absorb part of the load.

00:16:44.956 --> 00:16:45.936
In addition to this system

00:16:46.336 --> 00:16:52.998
2 enormous metal beams and 4 mega-pillars made of reinforced concrete onto which part of the load is transferred.

00:17:00.216 --> 00:17:01.236
Inside the stadium,

00:17:01.717 --> 00:17:06.040
The two mega-beams located just below the retractable roof can be easily identified.

00:17:12.987 --> 00:17:17.510
We can also see the eight pylons that pass through the top of the stands to anchor themselves to the ground.

00:17:19.492 --> 00:17:20.634
But neither the megabeams,

00:17:20.913 --> 00:17:22.915
nor do the pylons obstruct the spectators' view.

00:17:23.675 --> 00:17:26.038
even those who are watching the match from the top of the stands.

00:17:29.555 --> 00:17:33.601
The idea of ​​these eight pylons, which function like guy wires, did not come from nowhere.

00:17:34.523 --> 00:17:40.211
The architect Kurokawa had already used a similar system for one of his previous buildings,

00:17:41.052 --> 00:17:42.154
the Toyota Stadium.

00:17:53.209 --> 00:17:57.811
It is indeed the same system as the one used for the Toyota Stadium near Nagoya.

00:17:58.452 --> 00:18:00.374
But this one only has 4 pylons,

00:18:00.973 --> 00:18:02.915
whereas the one in Saint Petersburg has 8.

00:18:05.798 --> 00:18:06.317
Technically...

00:18:06.817 --> 00:18:09.641
It would have been simpler to manufacture them with an external orientation.

00:18:11.062 --> 00:18:14.205
But Kurokawa wanted the masts to point towards the sky.

00:18:19.209 --> 00:18:22.872
The local engineers asked us several times to turn them outwards instead.

00:18:23.471 --> 00:18:24.273
But we refused.

00:18:25.074 --> 00:18:28.076
And it's thanks to that that we were able to achieve this aesthetic in the end.

00:18:34.367 --> 00:18:36.088
Thanks to this architectural feat,

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:40.073
The roof and the rest of the building appear to be disconnected from each other.

00:18:45.217 --> 00:18:47.219
The roof thus appears to almost float in the air.

00:18:47.719 --> 00:18:52.182
offering a further similarity to the flying saucer envisioned by the architect.

00:18:55.746 --> 00:18:56.865
If in Saint Petersburg,

00:18:57.287 --> 00:19:02.250
The workers and engineers had to find solutions to bring the Japanese architect's imagination to life.

00:19:05.048 --> 00:19:05.488
In Baku,

00:19:06.228 --> 00:19:07.629
the manufacturers had to cope,

00:19:07.729 --> 00:19:07.849
them,

00:19:08.189 --> 00:19:09.049
to other challenges.

00:19:10.130 --> 00:19:10.970
The most complex,

00:19:11.631 --> 00:19:13.530
to ensure the stability of the building.

00:19:20.394 --> 00:19:21.095
First problem,

00:19:22.015 --> 00:19:27.037
The site chosen by the authorities to build the stadium is located on the shores of Lake Boyuxor.

00:19:29.118 --> 00:19:33.139
The location has the advantage of being situated between the international airport and the city center.

00:19:38.432 --> 00:19:42.413
It is therefore easily accessible for residents and for spectators from all over the world.

00:19:44.174 --> 00:19:49.616
The construction of the enclosure is part of a vast project to rehabilitate the lake and its surroundings.

00:19:50.656 --> 00:19:53.177
long exploited by the mining and oil industry.

00:19:57.239 --> 00:20:00.000
To such an extent that it seemed almost impossible to build on this coating.

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:02.521
We appreciate a stadium of such importance.

00:20:09.506 --> 00:20:11.926
The area where the stadium is located was really difficult,

00:20:12.067 --> 00:20:13.907
especially in terms of soil quality,

00:20:14.128 --> 00:20:16.410
because until now, people came there to extract oil.

00:20:18.871 --> 00:20:23.233
You could almost say that we are on the lake and that the stadium is built on very unstable ground.

00:20:26.355 --> 00:20:28.537
This was one of the biggest challenges for the construction.

00:20:30.518 --> 00:20:33.619
Designing the foundations required a great deal of inventiveness.

00:20:37.021 --> 00:20:40.443
In addition to its proximity to the lake and the poor soil quality,

00:20:41.163 --> 00:20:43.884
The location is in an area subject to very strong winds.

00:20:44.645 --> 00:20:45.025
Worse,

00:20:45.645 --> 00:20:47.246
It is even classified as a seismic zone.

00:20:50.201 --> 00:20:51.461
In the event of an earthquake,

00:20:51.902 --> 00:20:54.884
Seismic waves can generate forces known as uplift forces.

00:20:55.605 --> 00:20:56.045
In other words,

00:20:56.605 --> 00:21:00.528
The stadium could simply be ripped from the ground by the force of the earthquake.

00:21:01.769 --> 00:21:03.650
To ensure that the enclosure can withstand the stress,

00:21:04.431 --> 00:21:10.595
The engineers opted for a particular foundation system generally used for high-rise buildings.

00:21:11.976 --> 00:21:17.000
They were sunk into the ground just below the stadium using concrete piles reinforced with metal rods.

00:21:21.182 --> 00:21:22.923
Typically for this type of construction,

00:21:23.545 --> 00:21:26.947
Three or four piles are sufficient to guarantee the stability of the structure.

00:21:27.768 --> 00:21:28.409
But in this case,

00:21:29.069 --> 00:21:30.850
They decided to pull out all the stops.

00:21:39.711 --> 00:21:41.612
To avoid any structural problems,

00:21:42.513 --> 00:21:46.935
2500 reinforced concrete piles were installed before the construction of the enclosure.

00:21:48.656 --> 00:21:51.596
800 under the access ramps and the esplanade and

00:21:51.998 --> 00:21:52.738
1700 under the sand.

00:21:52.778 --> 00:21:53.399
the stadium itself.

00:21:55.961 --> 00:21:57.822
These piles are 1.20 m in diameter.

00:22:00.244 --> 00:22:10.132
They descend to a depth of 35 m and their summit is located just at ground level.

00:22:11.112 --> 00:22:12.933
Once the 2500 piles are completed,

00:22:13.594 --> 00:22:19.078
The area on which the stadium was to be built was covered with several layers up to a thickness of 3 m.

00:22:20.839 --> 00:22:21.800
Gravel first,

00:22:23.043 --> 00:22:24.585
then a first layer of concrete.

00:22:27.148 --> 00:22:29.611
Next comes a plastic film for insulation.

00:22:30.771 --> 00:22:33.855
Then a waterproofing fabric called geotextile.

00:22:34.797 --> 00:22:38.562
And finally, a last layer of reinforced concrete to cover everything.

00:22:40.183 --> 00:22:40.663
To finish,

00:22:41.384 --> 00:22:46.307
The building was constructed around a superstructure composed of 60 mega-pillars of concrete.

00:22:47.367 --> 00:22:52.109
A design that allows the Baku Olympic Stadium to withstand winds and earthquakes.

00:23:00.574 --> 00:23:03.174
But the engineers faced another challenge.

00:23:04.672 --> 00:23:08.915
The stadium was scheduled to be inaugurated in 2015 for the first European Games.

00:23:10.216 --> 00:23:12.438
And the work could not begin until 2013.

00:23:13.419 --> 00:23:16.001
It took barely more than two years to build such a structure,

00:23:16.761 --> 00:23:17.962
The challenge was immense.

00:23:22.017 --> 00:23:23.298
The deadlines were very short.

00:23:24.939 --> 00:23:27.360
We had to plan all the activities at the same time.

00:23:29.000 --> 00:23:29.721
Everything that mattered,

00:23:29.961 --> 00:23:30.903
It was about delivering on time.

00:23:32.043 --> 00:23:35.726
We needed to use all our resources in the most efficient way possible.

00:23:36.167 --> 00:23:37.248
including labor,

00:23:37.688 --> 00:23:39.911
the manufacturing of the components or the design.

00:23:41.273 --> 00:23:45.538
Construction began with 8 million cubic meters of backfilling and excavation.

00:23:48.001 --> 00:23:48.361
Afterwards,

00:23:48.362 --> 00:23:49.182
The concrete has been poured.

00:23:50.723 --> 00:23:53.825
360,000 m3 of concrete were poured on the site.

00:23:57.105 --> 00:23:58.185
To meet the deadlines,

00:23:58.745 --> 00:24:05.407
The construction site was divided into 8 identical zones, allowing several teams to work at the same time and to accelerate the pace of work.

00:24:14.770 --> 00:24:19.412
The components of the metal structure were prefabricated in a factory in Türkiye.

00:24:23.356 --> 00:24:24.837
In order to speed things up,

00:24:25.598 --> 00:24:30.182
55,000 tonnes of steel structures were manufactured in a factory in Türkiye.

00:24:30.962 --> 00:24:33.384
shipped to Baku and installed on site.

00:24:37.027 --> 00:24:41.533
The metal framework was then assembled on site by 600 welders.

00:24:43.755 --> 00:24:47.079
A considerable amount of material had to be transported to the site.

00:24:48.300 --> 00:24:52.286
Building within such tight deadlines was truly our biggest challenge.

00:25:04.000 --> 00:25:05.440
Around each area of ​​the construction site,

00:25:06.021 --> 00:25:08.541
as the concrete bleachers began to take shape,

00:25:09.082 --> 00:25:11.582
The metal sub-parts were assembled one by one,

00:25:13.383 --> 00:25:15.624
ready to be positioned on the building.

00:25:17.764 --> 00:25:19.025
First, the vertical elements,

00:25:19.745 --> 00:25:21.905
placed along the 60 mega-pillars of concrete.

00:25:24.806 --> 00:25:25.006
Then,

00:25:25.286 --> 00:25:26.586
the structural elements,

00:25:27.027 --> 00:25:27.927
to form the roof.

00:25:35.432 --> 00:25:41.076
Each piece was hoisted using mega-cranes capable of transporting more than 1200 tons of metal.

00:25:49.684 --> 00:25:53.587
Each element of the framework was then fixed to the top of the mega-pillars of concrete,

00:25:54.249 --> 00:25:56.670
then connected with the element located right next to it.

00:26:02.751 --> 00:26:09.638
A perfectly controlled organization which made it possible to complete the 28,000 m² of roof in exactly 210 days.

00:26:12.800 --> 00:26:17.585
The perimeter of the enclosure and the roof were then covered with an outer layer of ETFE.

00:26:18.186 --> 00:26:24.651
the same material as that used for the dome of the roof of Saint Petersburg which lets light into the stadium.

00:26:27.340 --> 00:26:29.701
The facade is designed with two layers of TFE.

00:26:30.021 --> 00:26:33.062
inside which LED lighting has been installed.

00:26:35.163 --> 00:26:37.344
The facade thus becomes a gigantic screen.

00:26:39.605 --> 00:26:40.125
In total,

00:26:40.525 --> 00:26:46.267
We managed to cover 28,000 m² of roof and 36,000 m² of facade in 24 months.

00:26:55.924 --> 00:26:59.068
By working 7 days a week and 24 hours a day,

00:26:59.710 --> 00:27:02.653
and above all by scrupulously respecting the schedule planned from the outset,

00:27:03.114 --> 00:27:06.258
We managed to build the stadium without changing the delivery date.

00:27:07.659 --> 00:27:08.881
And we finished on time.

00:27:16.119 --> 00:27:21.762
The Baku Olympic Stadium, with its 68,000 seats, was inaugurated on March 6, 2015.

00:27:22.482 --> 00:27:24.924
that is, three months before the start of the European Games.

00:27:35.819 --> 00:27:42.884
The whole world watched the opening ceremony of the European Games in the Batum Olympic Stadium.

00:27:43.785 --> 00:27:46.586
More than 200 television channels broadcast the event.

00:27:48.052 --> 00:27:48.393
And we,

00:27:48.493 --> 00:27:48.913
That's for sure.

00:27:49.533 --> 00:27:54.036
We were extremely proud of the comments we received from all countries regarding the quality of the stadium.

00:27:55.437 --> 00:27:55.717
In my opinion,

00:27:56.038 --> 00:27:58.099
It's a truly magnificent speaker.

00:27:58.960 --> 00:28:01.441
And it was built to a very high standard of quality.

00:28:02.881 --> 00:28:04.003
It is clear that in the future,

00:28:04.063 --> 00:28:07.807
Many other major sporting events will be able to be organized here.

00:28:08.829 --> 00:28:09.149
You know,

00:28:09.189 --> 00:28:12.873
We visited many stadiums in Europe before starting construction.

00:28:13.554 --> 00:28:16.638
And ours truly stands out thanks to its unique design.

00:28:16.658 --> 00:28:17.519
which is reminiscent of the city's construction.

00:28:17.680 --> 00:28:18.881
The flame and the fire.

00:28:21.282 --> 00:28:21.783
And for us,

00:28:22.203 --> 00:28:25.547
It is very important that this stadium represents these symbols of our history.

00:28:26.248 --> 00:28:29.750
An exceptional stadium,

00:28:30.432 --> 00:28:31.512
exceptional project.

00:28:32.973 --> 00:28:33.493
If in Baku,

00:28:33.673 --> 00:28:35.016
It lasted barely 26 months.

00:28:35.895 --> 00:28:36.916
in Saint Petersburg,

00:28:37.458 --> 00:28:38.699
the construction of the stadium,

00:28:38.858 --> 00:28:39.058
She,

00:28:39.400 --> 00:28:40.681
required a lot.

00:28:41.181 --> 00:28:42.102
much more time.

00:28:52.567 --> 00:28:53.067
In total,

00:28:53.848 --> 00:28:57.329
It took 11 years of work to build the Gazprom Arena.

00:29:01.011 --> 00:29:03.013
The cost of the project would exceed one billion euros.

00:29:03.854 --> 00:29:07.454
making the Saint Petersburg stadium one of the most expensive in history.

00:29:29.879 --> 00:29:33.442
Among the most amazing innovations found in this exceptional arena,

00:29:34.382 --> 00:29:38.144
One of them concerns one of the most important elements of a football stadium,

00:29:39.003 --> 00:29:39.504
his land.

00:29:48.608 --> 00:29:59.095
The entire 120-meter long by 80-meter wide pitch can be moved out of the enclosure and positioned on an outdoor space built to the exact dimensions of the pitch.

00:30:05.486 --> 00:30:12.255
An extremely complex maneuver that requires two days of preparation and that the stadium team only performs on very rare occasions.

00:30:21.096 --> 00:30:22.657
Since our stadium has a retractable roof,

00:30:23.636 --> 00:30:25.258
We don't move the field often.

00:30:25.918 --> 00:30:29.840
This only applies when we organize events that are not sporting events.

00:30:30.160 --> 00:30:31.621
concerts or other events,

00:30:31.921 --> 00:30:35.182
where it is necessary to bring a large audience onto the field.

00:30:35.923 --> 00:30:36.403
In that case,

00:30:36.982 --> 00:30:39.124
We cannot allow people onto the lawn.

00:30:39.163 --> 00:30:40.485
Otherwise they risk being damaged.

00:30:40.965 --> 00:30:43.846
Therefore, it is to preserve it that the field is moved outside.

00:30:49.336 --> 00:30:56.826
The ground moves thanks to a system composed of several traction modules that allow the enormous 6000-tonne structure to advance.

00:30:58.589 --> 00:31:06.159
Each module consists of two drive wheels on tires with a diameter of 1 meter that move at a speed of 5 cm per second.

00:31:10.752 --> 00:31:17.156
All modules are equipped with an electric motor and they are all synchronized to ensure the smoothest possible movement.

00:31:17.616 --> 00:31:18.117
In total,

00:31:18.498 --> 00:31:21.279
There are 16 modules at the front and 16 at the rear.

00:31:31.027 --> 00:31:37.070
But moving such a structure induces significant stresses at the points of contact between the wheels and the ground.

00:31:38.111 --> 00:31:38.734
Again,

00:31:39.235 --> 00:31:40.861
It required some ingenuity.

00:31:45.108 --> 00:31:46.549
To reduce the weight on the wheels,

00:31:46.989 --> 00:31:49.509
The engineers designed an air cushion system.

00:31:50.471 --> 00:31:52.252
When ground movement begins,

00:31:52.672 --> 00:31:56.874
The cushion is triggered, which lifts the ground and reduces the weight on the wheels.

00:31:57.574 --> 00:32:03.737
This reduces wear on the wheels and allows the terrain to be moved without fear of damaging the structure.

00:32:18.092 --> 00:32:21.564
This air cushion system is composed of 36 injection modules.

00:32:22.687 --> 00:32:27.971
They are installed at the front and rear of the field and are equipped with high-pressure fans.

00:32:29.652 --> 00:32:38.517
The fans allow 22 m3 of air per second to be injected into a sealed cavity located under the lawn and which occupies the entire perimeter of the field.

00:32:42.618 --> 00:32:43.418
In 30 minutes,

00:32:44.019 --> 00:32:50.582
the cavity is filled and makes it possible to almost completely compensate for the weight supported by the drive wheels of the traction modules.

00:32:53.416 --> 00:32:55.697
Thanks to sensors located around the structure,

00:32:56.257 --> 00:33:03.160
A centralized control system helps maintain uniform pressure in the cavity throughout the entire displacement process.

00:33:06.861 --> 00:33:08.922
The whole assembly can then slide effortlessly,

00:33:09.422 --> 00:33:10.783
but at a very slow speed

00:33:11.323 --> 00:33:12.123
outwards.

00:33:18.901 --> 00:33:22.202
And it takes an average of 4 hours for the terrain to reach its location.

00:33:24.864 --> 00:33:33.589
One of the most critical aspects of this extraordinary setup is the 80-meter-wide empty space created at the end of the field to allow the passage of the grass.

00:33:34.971 --> 00:33:39.894
Above rests the weight of the bleachers without any pillar being able to support the load.

00:33:47.044 --> 00:33:49.265
This is a truly unique part of the stadium.

00:33:49.944 --> 00:33:50.265
Actually,

00:33:50.684 --> 00:33:56.926
It's a bit like we're under a bridge made of reinforced concrete that has to support a very heavy load.

00:33:57.606 --> 00:34:00.268
Just above us is the fan zone.

00:34:00.907 --> 00:34:01.368
And of course,

00:34:01.409 --> 00:34:03.889
The fans are constantly jumping and moving around.

00:34:04.610 --> 00:34:10.891
That is why we have installed a monitoring system that measures the deformation of this structure during the match.

00:34:15.415 --> 00:34:22.838
The case of this stand at the Gazprom Arena shows how much the structures of modern mega-stadiums must withstand the strongest stresses.

00:34:32.662 --> 00:34:33.102
In Baku,

00:34:33.783 --> 00:34:36.644
given the risk of earthquakes in the region,

00:34:37.364 --> 00:34:42.346
The venue was even equipped with a state-of-the-art earthquake detection system.

00:34:44.311 --> 00:34:48.353
The last major earthquake struck Azerbaijan on November 25, 2000.

00:34:49.414 --> 00:34:51.916
With a magnitude of 6.8 on the Richter scale,

00:34:52.456 --> 00:34:55.737
Its epicenter was located near the coasts of the Caspian Sea.

00:34:56.137 --> 00:34:59.619
just 25 km southeast of Baku city centre.

00:35:00.800 --> 00:35:05.485
The fire caused the deaths of around thirty people and damage to more than 90 buildings in the city.

00:35:06.184 --> 00:35:10.628
The authorities therefore preferred not to take any risks during the construction of the stadium.

00:35:15.432 --> 00:35:26.262
Seismic wave sensors have therefore been installed all around the stadium to detect the slightest tremor and immediately send the information to the control center located inside the stadium.

00:35:39.373 --> 00:35:41.294
This is what we call our magic box.

00:35:42.615 --> 00:35:42.995
Actually,

00:35:43.556 --> 00:35:44.976
This is the seismic warning system.

00:35:47.199 --> 00:35:50.520
This system allows information to be received in less than 8 seconds.

00:35:53.063 --> 00:35:56.586
So if the epicenter of the earthquake is located 120 km from the stadium,

00:35:57.387 --> 00:36:00.512
The information will be transmitted to this box in just 24 seconds.

00:36:04.997 --> 00:36:07.280
So it only takes 24 seconds to...

00:36:07.280 --> 00:36:12.767
so that the alarm sounds throughout the stadium and the device triggers a general shutdown of the venue.

00:36:14.169 --> 00:36:19.737
The backup generators then kick in and all electrical systems are switched over to the generators.

00:36:21.219 --> 00:36:21.559
Gas,

00:36:21.619 --> 00:36:21.980
him too.

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:22.360
is cut off.

00:36:27.387 --> 00:36:31.369
It is in this ultra-secure space that all the stadium's systems are managed.

00:36:32.090 --> 00:36:32.671
Heating,

00:36:33.070 --> 00:36:33.650
lighting,

00:36:34.092 --> 00:36:36.952
Video surveillance or even lawn irrigation.

00:36:37.733 --> 00:36:39.914
Welcome to a fully connected stadium.

00:36:40.855 --> 00:36:42.336
a football 3.0 stadium.

00:36:46.838 --> 00:36:48.619
Since its inauguration in 2015,

00:36:49.240 --> 00:36:52.442
This ultra-modern venue has become the symbol of a new Azerbaijan.

00:36:52.961 --> 00:36:54.423
open to the world and to the future.

00:36:55.802 --> 00:36:56.463
Inside,

00:36:56.903 --> 00:37:02.335
Every detail has been considered to ensure that the Baku Olympic Stadium impresses visitors from all over the world.

00:37:11.417 --> 00:37:16.178
The interior of the stadium has been designed to create a very comfortable atmosphere.

00:37:17.798 --> 00:37:18.919
with clean lines.

00:37:20.860 --> 00:37:23.539
The atmosphere is very bright and the colours are very pleasant.

00:37:24.260 --> 00:37:27.201
The decor blends ancient and modern influences.

00:37:27.682 --> 00:37:28.882
a bit like the stadium itself.

00:37:30.883 --> 00:37:31.202
Actually,

00:37:31.763 --> 00:37:34.423
Every single element of the stadium reflects this philosophy.

00:37:38.280 --> 00:37:41.742
Our stadium is not only the official home of the national football team,

00:37:42.523 --> 00:37:47.686
but it is also a multifunctional center where we can host different types of events.

00:37:49.007 --> 00:37:51.649
It can range from small events like parties or birthdays.

00:37:52.190 --> 00:37:53.791
up to major international events.

00:37:56.010 --> 00:37:56.631
And of course,

00:37:57.112 --> 00:38:03.514
We are very proud to show everyone the quality of our facilities and the services we can offer our visitors.

00:38:04.374 --> 00:38:05.434
whether they are VIPs,

00:38:06.753 --> 00:38:07.335
fans,

00:38:07.695 --> 00:38:08.454
journalists,

00:38:09.055 --> 00:38:11.056
players and, of course, athletes.

00:38:16.105 --> 00:38:19.186
The stadium has a capacity of 68,700 seats.

00:38:19.686 --> 00:38:21.706
which makes our stadium the largest in the region.

00:38:22.728 --> 00:38:28.449
We have 126 VIP suites and 6 tiers of grandstand seating available for everyone.

00:38:39.916 --> 00:38:45.720
The stadiums in Baku and Saint Petersburg are therefore two perfect examples of what stadiums of the future should become.

00:38:47.381 --> 00:38:51.504
Forget the old sports arena of the past where only the pitch and the stands mattered.

00:38:52.464 --> 00:38:52.884
Today,

00:38:53.625 --> 00:38:57.367
A stadium must be able to accommodate the public in the best possible conditions of comfort.

00:39:04.199 --> 00:39:04.980
Yuri Fedotov,

00:39:05.380 --> 00:39:07.824
the head of security at the Gazprom Arena,

00:39:08.445 --> 00:39:11.327
takes us to one of the most secret places within the compound,

00:39:11.807 --> 00:39:13.770
Access to the stands is prohibited for spectators.

00:39:24.884 --> 00:39:27.886
We are in what is called the presidential box.

00:39:29.427 --> 00:39:29.808
For us,

00:39:30.429 --> 00:39:32.329
This is the most important place in the stadium.

00:39:33.610 --> 00:39:37.733
This box was specially built for VIPs who come to watch the matches, and in addition to that,

00:39:37.735 --> 00:39:37.953
for the fans.

00:39:37.954 --> 00:39:45.756
in particular heads of state.

00:39:49.937 --> 00:39:53.978
Given that everyone in this box has security personnel,

00:39:54.659 --> 00:40:00.000
Additional measures have been taken to ensure the maximum safety of these individuals.

00:40:00.079 --> 00:40:04.400
within the compound.

00:40:05.001 --> 00:40:12.382
All their movements were planned and we made sure they did not have to cross paths with other spectators on their way to the box.

00:40:15.784 --> 00:40:20.324
They therefore have reserved access to the stadiums and special elevator systems.

00:40:22.186 --> 00:40:22.766
And of course,

00:40:23.126 --> 00:40:26.527
Very specific evacuation measures have been put in place.

00:40:26.927 --> 00:40:29.807
From the very beginning of the war,

00:40:29.807 --> 00:40:31.088
of the stadium construction,

00:40:31.789 --> 00:40:40.197
One of the first missions was to study the construction of this lodge in accordance with the police forces and special services.

00:40:41.159 --> 00:40:46.485
It was under their supervision that the project was conceived and every last detail was considered.

00:40:53.451 --> 00:40:55.673
But regardless of the quality of the dressing rooms and backstage areas,

00:40:56.213 --> 00:40:59.836
and the technologies used to modernize these 21st-century stadiums,

00:41:00.597 --> 00:41:01.759
the key location for a stadium,

00:41:02.338 --> 00:41:04.320
the one around which everything must be designed

00:41:05.041 --> 00:41:05.321
It's him.

00:41:06.121 --> 00:41:06.623
the field.

00:41:12.627 --> 00:41:14.009
This is where the show takes place.

00:41:14.849 --> 00:41:16.670
where the heroes of the stadium clash.

00:41:18.007 --> 00:41:18.347
And here,

00:41:18.427 --> 00:41:19.429
in northern Russia,

00:41:19.808 --> 00:41:22.490
to ensure the quality of play by the teams,

00:41:23.070 --> 00:41:25.692
The lawn requires very special attention.

00:41:30.815 --> 00:41:34.176
Because, given the climatic conditions and the design of the stadium,

00:41:34.757 --> 00:41:37.498
A completely natural lawn would be far too vulnerable.

00:41:44.255 --> 00:41:47.757
Tatiana Makarova is the agronomist in charge of the stadium's turf.

00:41:53.882 --> 00:42:03.869
Conditions here are extremely difficult because the roof is closed and daylight and sunlight do not pass well through the roof.

00:42:04.288 --> 00:42:05.570
The club therefore had to buy a...

00:42:05.570 --> 00:42:10.711
additional lighting is provided on the field 24 hours a day to compensate for the lack of sunlight.

00:42:13.372 --> 00:42:17.452
In addition,

00:42:17.454 --> 00:42:18.553
The building is locked down.

00:42:18.952 --> 00:42:20.613
Air circulation is difficult.

00:42:21.173 --> 00:42:27.495
We therefore have 16 fans at our disposal which allow the grass to grow in good conditions of aeration and humidity.

00:42:36.460 --> 00:42:39.280
But the real secret of the stadium's pitch lies elsewhere,

00:42:40.201 --> 00:42:41.202
beneath the lawn itself,

00:42:42.142 --> 00:42:44.643
composed of a mixture of natural and synthetic turf.

00:42:50.445 --> 00:42:51.726
This system is fundamental.

00:42:53.206 --> 00:42:53.686
First of all,

00:42:53.867 --> 00:42:56.668
Using natural grass is a demand from footballers.

00:42:56.867 --> 00:42:58.608
who prefer to play on this type of grass.

00:42:59.289 --> 00:43:02.369
And they get injured much less often than on completely artificial turf.

00:43:05.471 --> 00:43:08.493
So we use what is called a hybrid system.

00:43:10.675 --> 00:43:11.235
Under the grass,

00:43:11.615 --> 00:43:14.337
Synthetic elements stabilize the upper part.

00:43:15.318 --> 00:43:15.838
And above,

00:43:15.858 --> 00:43:16.400
It's natural.

00:43:17.900 --> 00:43:20.181
This is somewhat the new way of growing grass.

00:43:22.643 --> 00:43:29.536
The importance of the pitch to the quality of a football match and the spectacle offered to fans has given rise to a true science of turf.

00:43:30.857 --> 00:43:33.261
It all starts at the junction between the ground and the terrain.

00:43:36.895 --> 00:43:37.375
First of all,

00:43:38.076 --> 00:43:45.821
Polystyrene foam with thermal insulation and waterproofing properties is placed to insulate the ground from the soil and prevent freezing.

00:43:47.842 --> 00:43:53.527
The trenches dug in the moss then allow for the installation of channels to heat the ground and prevent mold.

00:43:55.027 --> 00:43:59.652
Then deposit a mixture of sand and gravel which serves as the base for a synthetic substrate.

00:44:00.511 --> 00:44:04.454
A kind of soil that will provide the grass with ideal oxygenation conditions.

00:44:06.315 --> 00:44:10.960
Next comes a support made of synthetic filaments sewn onto a cotton fabric.

00:44:12.020 --> 00:44:16.943
It is in turn covered with the same substrate on which the natural grass seeds will be sown.

00:44:18.286 --> 00:44:24.049
The stadium pitch is therefore a mixed pitch in which natural grass and synthetic fibers are combined.

00:44:30.376 --> 00:44:30.896
In my life,

00:44:31.636 --> 00:44:32.076
this lawn,

00:44:32.136 --> 00:44:33.877
He's a bit like a member of my family.

